+# .space
+
+Everything that makes this fork differ from [abue-ammar/tinycast](https://github.com/abue-ammar/tinycast).
+`main` is never edited by hand beyond this folder: it is regenerated as *upstream main + these patches*,
+one commit per patch (titled after it, its row below as the message), then one commit with this folder,
+the README and `apply.sh`'s rewrites.
+
+| File | What it does |
+| --- | --- |
+| `patches/0001-alias-space.patch` | An exact, case-sensitive user alias + Space opens its entry: rows with inline arguments focus the first unanswered field (or the first field, when every one is optional); an extension view command whose arguments are all optional opens instead, so what follows lands in its own search bar (`brew` → Search Homebrew); everything else runs (apps and settings panes keep searching). A backslash right before the Space escapes it into a plain space. It fires only with the caret at the end of the query and nothing selected (read from the field editor), so a Space typed mid-query stays a space (idea from [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/4141ac68)). |
+| `patches/0002-updater-and-links.patch` | The in-app updater and the About link point at this fork; About shows a "✨ Space Edition" chip and reads "Tinycast Space Edition". |
+| `patches/0004-querystring-node-coercion.patch` | Extension runtime: `querystring.stringify` coerces `undefined`/`null` to `""` like Node. Without it google-auth-library sends `client_secret=undefined` and Google answers `invalid_client` for any client without a secret (e.g. 2FA Code Finder's Gmail sign-in). `apply.sh` rebuilds `RaycastRuntime.generated.js` after it. |
+| `patches/0005-external-hyper-glyph.patch` | Settings → General → Hyper Key: with Hyper Key set to None, "Show ✦ for another app's Hyper key" collapses the Hyper chord to ✦ anyway (for Karabiner/Hyperkey-style remappers) and keeps Include Shift editable. |
+| `patches/0006-inline-alias-shortcut-editing.patch` | ⌘K on a launcher entry gains *Change Alias* and *Change Shortcut* rows that edit in place (extension commands included). Ported from [jhasubhash/tinycast](https://github.com/jhasubhash/tinycast/commit/f509d005) (AGPL-3.0); everything lives in the new `InlineEntryEditor.swift`, the rest is one-line hooks marked `tinycast-space`. `apply.sh` regenerates `project.pbxproj` with XcodeGen for the added file instead of patching it. |
+| `patches/0008-buffer-blob-file.patch` | Extension runtime: `require("buffer")` exposes `Blob` and `File`, as Node's does. Undici subclasses them, so extensions bundling it (Google Translate) crashed on load with "The superclass is not a constructor". |
+| `patches/0009-undici-fetch-dispatcher.patch` | Extension runtime: a bundled undici finds a dispatcher already installed in its global slot (`Symbol.for("undici.globalDispatcher.1")`) that sends every request through Tinycast's `fetch` bridge, so it never reaches for `net` (no sockets, no Node). `stream` gains Node's `isDisturbed`/`isErrored`/`isReadable` probes, which undici asks before reading a body. Google Translate is the reference case. If undici ever renames the slot, it falls back to the old "`net.isIP` is not supported" error, nothing worse. |
+| `patches/0011-raycast-themes.patch` | Raycast themes, as Raycast does them. Settings → General → Appearance has a *Light theme* and a *Dark theme* slot; the appearance Tinycast draws in (System follows macOS) picks between them. Each slot opens a browser of that appearance's themes — ray.so's catalog (`RaycastThemeCatalog.swift`, generated by `tools/raycast-themes.py`, MIT notice included) plus imported ones — under a live preview of the hovered theme. A *Theme* command lists the installed themes and previews each one on the window as it is highlighted: it is a small extension Tinycast writes into its own extensions folder at launch (`RaycastThemeCommand.swift`, fed `assets/themes.json`), so no palette mode or command enum changes. A theme swaps hues, never alphas: the ink ramp takes its `text`, the selection fill its `selection`, the palette's backdrop Raycast's gradient from `background` to `backgroundSecondary` (70 % down, as ray.so draws it; *Theme background*, `spaceRaycastThemeBackgroundOpacity`, default 70 %), floating glass (menus, the action capsule) a tint of `background`, other surfaces' scrim `background`, and extension `Color.Red` and friends its named colors. Tokens read an observable revision as they are drawn, so a theme change redraws exactly the views showing a themed color, in place and without an appearance flash. A `raycast://theme` link — outside, *Import Link from Clipboard*, or an extension's `open()` — asks in a dialog (Use Theme / Just Add / Cancel) over the palette, and the `closeMainWindow` Raycast Explorer sends right after is skipped; the Theme command's own links carry `apply=1` and switch at once. While an extension row whose `Action.Open` targets a theme link is highlighted, the palette alone shows that theme (the runtime now passes `Action.Open`'s `target` as a prop). The core (`RaycastThemeCore.swift`) is AppKit/SwiftUI-only because `Theme.swift` reads it and harnesses compile `Theme.swift` alone. The extension bridge also hands `raycast://confetti` to patch 0007 now — an extension's confetti link used to just reopen the launcher. Upstream declined themes (abue-ammar/tinycast#640). |
+| `patches/0013-node-process-and-streams.patch` | Extension runtime: a missing executable fails as Node's `spawn <cmd> ENOENT` (code, errno, syscall, path, spawnargs) on `spawn`'s `error` event, `execFile` callbacks and promises and `spawnSync`'s `error`, and bare names resolve on the caller's `env.PATH` first (abue-ammar/tinycast#1585; after [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/70d5e5d563)). The gaps `got` hits (#1592): `prependOnceListener`, `ClientRequest.end([chunk][, encoding][, cb])` with `finish`, `read()` on an ended stream emitting `end`, `highWaterMark: 0` no longer stalling, and an `http.ServerResponse` class for got's `instanceof` check in `pipe`. Swift: `ExtensionNodeShims`/`ExtensionFetcher` for the PATH lookup and error fields. |
+| `patches/0014-extension-ui-parity.patch` | Extension screens: ⌘↵ runs the action panel's second action unless it has its own shortcut, sits in a submenu, or another action claims ⌘↵ (the ⌘K panel labels the first two ↵ and ⌘↵; forms keep ⌘↵ = submit) (#793). `context` in `raycast://extensions/…` deeplinks becomes the command's `launchContext` (#1452). A Form's `autoFocus` focuses after a `Task.yield()`, the pattern of upstream #1369 (#1495). `ExtensionScreen` and its rows drop `Equatable`, which made SwiftUI diff whole lists on every ↑/↓ (from [Tukks/tinycast](https://github.com/Tukks/tinycast/commit/dce96bb97b)). `IconCache.artwork` decodes `name@dark.ext` when the surface is dark and the file exists; a surface change already purges the cache, so one bitmap per icon is held (after [jhasubhash/tinycast](https://github.com/jhasubhash/tinycast/commit/0f77def63f)). |
+| `patches/0015-alias-tab.patch` | Tab on an exact alias does what patch 0001's Space does: 0001's handler takes both keys, and sits after upstream's Tab handler so it is asked first. Any other Tab keeps upstream's paths (fields, quicklink arguments, the launcher → clipboard → AI cycle). Declined upstream (#1594); asked for in this fork's #16. Same caret rule as 0001. |
+| `patches/0016-launcher-keys.patch` | With a query typed (when no favorite is pinned), ⌘1–⌘9 run the Nth entry row as Return would, with ⌘-held hints in the favorites' keycap style (#1357 and friends). `PaletteCoordinator.togglePalette` hides a visible palette on any screen, and `restoreAnyMode` brings that screen back (#1113, #1356; as [songhyun-k/tinycast](https://github.com/songhyun-k/tinycast/commit/aa5667d064)). |
+| `patches/0017-typo-tolerant-search.patch` | `LauncherOrder.ranked` scores a second time with typos allowed only when the first pass matched nothing, so every query that matches today ranks exactly as upstream ranks it. Bounded Damerau–Levenshtein against title word starts (none under 4 letters, 1 edit up to 7, titles ≤ 64 units), ordered by distance then frecency; `fuzz-test` covers it. After [arthur-fontaine/smallcast](https://github.com/arthur-fontaine/smallcast/commit/cb0a236245). |
+| `patches/0018-entry-deeplinks.patch` | `tinycast://open?id=<percent-encoded AppEntry.id>` runs a launcher entry through `LauncherCoordinator.launch`, as Return does (snippets expand at the caret instead); unknown ids show a HUD. Routed in `AppCore.handleOpenURL` after confetti and themes. Every entry's ⌘K menu gets *Copy Deeplink* (extension commands copy `tinycast://extensions/<owner>/<ext>/<cmd>`). No `arguments` are read, meetings and query-driven commands get no link, and system actions keep their confirmations. New `EntryDeepLink.swift`, `EntryDeepLinkActions.swift`, `entry-deeplink-test`. Declined upstream (#1005). A link that activated Tinycast first hands focus back (`NSApp.deactivate()`, then up to 500 ms for another app to come forward; no observer), so window commands, snippets and paste act on the app the link came from (after [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/b82afd94)). |
+| `patches/0019-clipboard-image-files.patch` | *Images Only* includes file entries whose extension is an image (and *Files Only* excludes them); the OCR search checks it in SQL through an `is_image_file` function, so its LIMIT counts only the filter's rows. From [mourato/tinycast-space](https://github.com/mourato/tinycast-space/commit/a211b371). |
+| `patches/0020-snippet-copy-and-save.patch` | Search Snippets: *Copy to Clipboard* (⌘↵) expands like Paste (arguments prompt included) and copies; *Show in Finder* moves to ⌘F (#1595). Clipboard History: *Save as Snippet* (⌘S, text entries, snippets on) opens the snippet editor with the text filled in (#1333). Save or Cancel in that editor returns to Clipboard History with the same query, filter and entry (`PaletteFrame.clipboardFilter`, found again by id); ⌘S is ignored while composing; the editor starts in Name (after [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/d8f04c29)). |
+| `patches/0021-app-show-info.patch` | ⌘I on an application row, and *Show Info in Finder* under *Show in Finder* in its ⌘K menu, open Finder's Get Info through upstream's own `AppLauncher.showInfoInFinder` (the Uninstall screen's route, Apple events to Finder); a refused Automation permission shows upstream's notice. Meetings keep ⌘I (#1326, declined upstream). |
+| `patches/0022-node-http-tables.patch` | Extension runtime: `http`/`https` `STATUS_CODES` and `METHODS` hold Node's tables instead of `{}` and `[]`, so extensions that list status codes or methods work. From [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/b7c96aab). |
+| `patches/0023-oauth-sign-in-recovery.patch` | Extension OAuth: `ExtensionSignInSession` settles exactly once — a browser session that fails to start throws `.failedToStart` instead of hanging `authorize()`, late callbacks after a cancel are ignored, a cancelled task never opens the browser — and `oauth.js` queues concurrent `authorize()` calls instead of refusing the second. New `ext-sign-in-test`. After [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/9ce7788f). |
+| `patches/0024-currency-fetch-race.patch` | Calculator: `CurrencyRateStore` drops a rate fetch that a newer one superseded (the daily pump and the refresh button can overlap), so older rates never overwrite fresher ones. From [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/661c57f8). |
+| `patches/0025-faster-lists-and-launch.patch` | `DateBucket.Boundaries` resolves Today, Yesterday, this week and this month once per list instead of per row (Clipboard History, Calculator history, AI Chat history and sidebar); the launch-at-login status, an XPC round trip of ~40 ms, is read off the main thread at launch, and a write cancels that read. Two parts of [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/de308447); its palette prewarm is left out, since it moves the open palette's memory into idle. |
+| `patches/0026-update-check-errors.patch` | A failed *Check for Updates* reports the check and its cause — offline or another URL error, GitHub's rate limit (429, or 403 with `X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0` / `Retry-After`), or the HTTP status — instead of a failed download (`UpdateFailure.checkFailed`, `check()` throws); a check already running says so. The message half of [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/0fee6712). |
+| `patches/0027-clipboard-number-slots.patch` | Clipboard History: ⌘1–⌘9 open the Nth visible row as Return would. Pins lead the list and keep their slots (⌘0 still opens a tenth pin); unpinned rows carry the count on, with digits after upstream's 400 ms hold. After [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/96377314), without its instant reveal. |
+| `patches/0028-settings-search-prefix.patch` | `?` or `?text` in the launcher searches Tinycast's own settings through upstream's `SettingsSearchCatalog` (new `SettingsSearchScreen.swift`): a bare `?` lists the panes, ↵ opens Settings at the pane or row, ⌘1–⌘9 open the Nth row, and File Search stays out of it. After [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/f337e4ea). |
+| `patches/0029-dictionary-suggestions.patch` | Dictionary: a word with no definition offers up to eight spelling suggestions (`NSSpellChecker`, only touched on a miss): ↵ looks it up, ⌥↵ copies it, ⌘↵ opens it in Dictionary.app. New `dictionary-session-test`. After [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/d28e810d). |
+| `patches/0030-file-search-folder-scope.patch` | File Search: Tab on a folder searches inside it (a chip beside the field; click, Esc or Backspace on an empty query leaves; *Search in Folder* in its ⌘K menu; an empty query lists the folder), through upstream's `FileIndexSnapshot.subtree`. A newer query cancels the running scan (no debounce, as upstream decided). After [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/1a5d0100). |
+| `README.fork.md` | Becomes the repository's `README.md`; `apply.sh` keeps upstream's README verbatim as `README.upstream.md` with a one-line note on top. Never a patch, so upstream README edits can't conflict. |
+| `patches/0007-confetti.patch` | Confetti as a system action and as `raycast://confetti`, drawn by the new `ConfettiOverlay.swift` with `CAEmitterLayer` (plus the undocumented `plane` particle type and `drag`/`wave` behaviours the effect needs, each applied defensively). Tunable live through `confetti.*` defaults. With Reduce motion on nothing animates: a burst on screen closes and a 🎉 HUD shows instead, for the command and the link alike (as [mSarheed/pipcast](https://github.com/mSarheed/pipcast/commit/9e8dd60a) does). |
+| `apply.sh` | Applies the patches in order with `git apply --3way` (with `SPACE_COMMIT=1`, as the workflows run it, committing each one together with the runtime bundle and Xcode project it regenerates; with `SPACE_REFRESH=1` as well, as the sync runs it, re-cutting each patch from its commit so the patches on `main` always match today's upstream and name blobs `main` keeps — the next `--3way` can then merge lines upstream moved instead of needing them verbatim), then points any upstream releases-page link (the Changelog menu item) at this fork, relaxes the system-action harness's hard-coded catalog size (patch 0007 adds one), lists patch 0011's theme core beside `Theme.swift` in every harness that compiles it, and turns `Theme.Colors`' one-line `static let x = ramp(…)` tokens into computed `static var`s so patch 0011 can redraw them through observation — rewrites, not patches, so a tag without those lines still applies and a harness upstream adds later is covered. |
+| `tools/raycast-themes.py` | Regenerates patch 0011's bundled theme catalog from raycast/ray-so. |
+| `gate.sh` | Release build + upstream's `Scripts/run-tests.sh`. A harness that also fails on the pristine upstream commit is ignored. |
+| `check-apply.sh` | The patch loop alone, on a throwaway worktree: the sync's Linux check runs it before a macOS runner is spent. On a conflict it names the patch and files, shows the conflict, and lists the upstream commits since `UPSTREAM` that touched those files. |
+| `report.sh` | Opens / closes the "blocked" issue. A conflict with the same cause on a newer upstream only retitles it, so one conflict notifies once. |
+| `UPSTREAM` | The upstream commit `main` was last built from. |
+
+## Automation
+
+- **`space-sync.yml`** — every 10 minutes checks upstream `main`. On a new commit (or a manual commit on top
+  of the generated one) it first applies the patches on Linux (`check-apply.sh`); a conflict goes to the
+  `space-sync` issue and stops there. Otherwise it rebuilds `main` = upstream + patches on macOS, builds,
+  runs the tests and force-pushes `main` with the patches re-cut against that upstream. On failure nothing
+  is pushed and the issue is opened; a hand-made push to `main` during the build just drops the result.
+- **`space-release.yml`** — twice an hour checks upstream's latest stable release. For a tag not yet released
+  here it applies the patches to that tag, builds, tests, signs with this fork's `Tinycast Self-Signed`
+  identity and publishes the same tag with a DMG and the zip the in-app updater installs.
+
+Upstream's own workflows (`release.yml`, `website*.yml`, `triage.yml`, `coauthors.yml`) are disabled in this
+repository's Actions settings.
+
+Secrets: `SIGNING_P12_BASE64`, `SIGNING_P12_PASSWORD` (the signing identity, never rotate it casually —
+installed copies only accept updates signed with the same certificate) and `SPACE_PUSH_TOKEN`
+(fine-grained token for this repository: Contents + Workflows read/write).
+
+## Changing the patch
+
+Start from the current `main`: its patches are fresh and each one is a commit there. Change the code on
+top of that patch's commit, re-cut the file with `git diff --full-index <commit>~1 <commit> -- . ':!Tinycast.xcodeproj'
+':!Tinycast/Resources/RaycastRuntime.generated.js' > .space/patches/…`, check that every patch still applies
+with plain `git apply` on upstream `main`, commit, and push; the next sync rebuilds `main` with it.
+
+What the sync's failures since September taught (most were a patch meeting an upstream change):
+
+- When upstream ships what a patch does, drop the patch and its rows here — the conflict is the signal.
+  The issue lists the upstream commits that touched the conflicting file to make that quick.
+- Put new code in new files and keep the hunks in upstream files to a hook of a line or two. Add lines
+  rather than rewrite upstream's; a value upstream keeps bumping is a rewrite in `apply.sh`, not a hunk.
+  When `private` members keep the code in an upstream file, it goes in an `extension` after the type
+  (0001 in `RootPaletteView.swift`). When a model or coordinator can carry a feature, its hooks go there
+  rather than into a view (0030 keeps its folder in `PaletteState` and `FileSearchSession`).
+  The busiest upstream files are `RootPaletteView.swift`, `AppCore.swift`, `SettingsSearchCatalog.swift`,
+  `PaletteWindowController.swift`, `Scripts/run-tests.sh` and the runtime's `fixtures.mjs`.
+- Add at most a one-line modifier to upstream's long SwiftUI chains (`stateObservers`, `keyHandlers`),
+  its body a call into the fork's code: CI's Xcode 26 gives up type-checking a chain that a newer Xcode
+  still builds. Of one view's `onKeyPress` handlers the one later in the chain is asked first, so a fork
+  handler that must see a key before upstream's goes after it.
+- A test the fork adds never depends on wall-clock timing: CI runners are slow and loaded, and a harness
+  whose upstream checks also flake upstream is ignored as a whole by `gate.sh`.
